From 73c0e8249f2fed3d4cfef38c50e56e456c8383bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:50:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 818/822] perf(dsv41): optimize decode GEMM, linear, WO, MoE
 runner, mHC, and collectives

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-61 series applied through 0817.

Rationale: Uses contiguous FP8 weight packing in decode WO and GEMM/linear
kernels, schedules persistent L2 prefetch and PDL across decode stages, and
tunes MoE runner, mHC, and SparkNet/CUDA collective orchestration.

Quality implications: None; bit-identical WO split tiles, L2 schedule tests,
and PDL source verification pass.

Tests: pytest -q -p deepseek_models -p tests.kernels.deepseek_v41_pdl_sources tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_l2_schedule.py tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_wo.py

Upstream status: local candidate-61 patch
